No file picker on a console, so find the ROM by looking for it

`GetRomPathFromBox` opens a desktop file dialog through `portable-file-dialogs`,
which shells out to zenity or kdialog over pipe/fork/dup2. None of those exist on
this platform, and the header is the only part of the extractor that does not
compile for it - five errors, all from that one include.

It is also not wanted. There is no pointer to browse with and nowhere to browse
to: a ROM copied onto the console lands in the title's own directory. Declining
here sends the caller to `ManuallySearchForRomMatchingType`, which scans exactly
that directory, so the console path is the one upstream already provides for
machines without a dialog.
---
diff --git a/mm/2s2h/Extractor/Extract.cpp b/mm/2s2h/Extractor/Extract.cpp
index d3c7e42..0c2fdb1 100644
--- a/mm/2s2h/Extractor/Extract.cpp
+++ b/mm/2s2h/Extractor/Extract.cpp
@@ -5,7 +5,12 @@
 #pragma comment(lib, "Shlwapi.lib")
 #endif
 #include "Extract.h"
+#ifndef __PROSPERO__
+// Desktop file pickers, which shell out to zenity or kdialog through pipe/fork/dup2.
+// None of that exists on this platform and none of it is wanted: the ROM is found by
+// scanning the title's own directory.
 #include "portable-file-dialogs.h"
+#endif
 #include <ship/utils/binarytools/BitConverter.h>
 #include "build.h"
 
@@ -282,6 +287,12 @@ bool Extractor::GetRomPathFromBox() {
         return false;
     }
     mCurrentRomPath = nameBuffer;
+#elif defined(__PROSPERO__)
+    // No file picker here, and nothing to pick with: `portable-file-dialogs` runs zenity
+    // or kdialog through pipe/fork/dup2, none of which this platform has. Declining sends
+    // the caller to `ManuallySearchForRomMatchingType`, which scans the title's own
+    // directory - which is where a ROM copied onto the console lands anyway.
+    return false;
 #else
     auto selection = pfd::open_file("Select a file", mSearchPath, { "N64 Roms", "*.z64 *.n64 *.v64" }).result();
 
